    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by two high-upside plays against favorable matchups. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** leads the squad with a 73.66 efficiency score, buoyed by a significant +19% SP skill boost against a struggling pitcher in a hitter-friendly park. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** (70.22) is a mandatory start; despite a slight park penalty, his +13% SP skill advantage and high-leverage opportunity in the 5-hole make him an elite option. **Gunnar Henderson** remains a must-start despite facing a formidable arm, as his extreme park factor (+16%) and dynamic platoon upside keep his score at a robust 69.20. **Sam Antonacci** and **Heliot Ramos** also provide excellent value, with **Sam Antonacci** benefiting from a premium lead-off spot to maximize his contribution in our scarcest category, stolen bases.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was benching **Josh Jung**, who narrowly missed the cut with a 41.97 score. While his base projections remain competitive, the optimizer favored higher-floor options like **Nasim Nunez** and **Coby Mayo** due to the specific lineup placements and the weight assigned to daily efficiency in a 5x5 format. We are also closely monitoring the lineup situation for **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**; facing an elite arm like deGrom severely depresses his ceiling (48.20), highlighting the volatility inherent in our current roster configuration. We continue to manage our remaining bench depth, including **Kyle Tucker**, who remains unavailable, while placeholders like **Jordan Westburg**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Dominic Smith**, **Brayan Rocchio**, **Curtis Mead**, **Liam Hicks**, **Luis Lara**, **Franklin Arias**, **Tommy White**, and **Henry Bolte** wait for upcoming opportunities to improve our category coverage. Investors should note that **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Andy Pages** remain sidelined on the IL, limiting our late-game tactical flexibility.",
